      ],
      "note": "Four checks fail at once. `expected_first_fail` follows the rule in `first_fail()`: the lowest check number that fails, so S5 comes before S7, S8 and S12. The printed report orders checks differently (S11, S1, S2, S3, S4, S12, S7, S8, S5, S6 on this package), so a reader who takes the first FAIL line in the report would name S12. Both are true statements about different orderings; the set above is authoritative and neither ordering is a severity ranking."
